# The harbour's words (docs/systems/jobs.md): its goals, the thief's pencil
# notes, the texts of its readables, and the gate up to the old town.
# Every text in <<...>> is still to write; replace it, keep the rest.

# Goals

== goal seal
kind: main
done: took(the_seal)
intent: The job itself: the harbourmaster's seal, in his office in the customs house.
text: <<take the seal>>

== goal up
kind: main
shows: done(seal)
done: arrived(old_town)
note: way_up
intent: Bring the seal up to the old town.
text: <<the onward goal>>

== goal captains_ring
kind: side
done: took(captains_ring)
intent: A special: the captain's ring, in the carrack's cabin strongbox.
text: <<the captain's ring>>

== goal signet
kind: side
done: took(signet)
intent: A special: a signet ring, hidden in the fort by the powder room.
text: <<the signet>>

# Pencil notes (the back of the letter)

== note tower_bell
intent: The lookout on the golden tower has a bell, and rings it at anything amiss.
text: <<pencil: the tower's bell>>

== note office_key
intent: The office key is kept on the customs house's ground floor.
text: <<pencil: the office key>>

== note dark_bays
intent: Some of the Ribeira arcade's bays are left dark; the lamps that go out get relit.
text: <<pencil: the arcade's dark bays>>

== note ways_up
intent: The ways up to the old town: the Sea Gate is shut and watched at night; the Guindais stair and the wall-walk.
text: <<pencil: the ways up>>

== note cabin_key
intent: The captain left his cabin key on the quay; his strongbox is in the cabin.
text: <<pencil: the cabin key>>

== note blowhole
intent: The blowhole's roar in the smugglers' cave covers sound.
text: <<pencil: the blowhole>>

== note powder_room
intent: There is something hidden behind the fort's powder room.
text: <<pencil: the powder room>>

== note way_up
intent: With the seal in hand: up to the old town, and why the seal matters there.
text: <<pencil: the way up>>

# Readables (their markers in the harbour name these slots)

== readable night_orders
note: tower_bell
intent: The harbour's night orders, pinned by the golden tower's door: the tower lookout rings the bell at anything amiss; lamps stay lit and are relit.
text:
<<the night orders>>

== readable duty_orders
note: office_key
intent: The customs watchman's duty orders on his desk: his round, and that the office key stays on the ground floor.
text:
<<the duty orders>>

== readable curfew
note: ways_up
intent: A curfew notice in the Terreiro arcade: the Sea Gate shut and watched at night; anyone going up by the Guindais stair or the wall.
text:
<<the curfew notice>>

== readable captains_log
note: cabin_key
intent: A page of the captain's log in the carrack's cabin: the strongbox, and the cabin key left with the quay.
text:
<<the captain's log>>

== readable smugglers_scrawl
note: blowhole
intent: A smugglers' scrawl on the cave beach: they move and talk only when the blowhole roars.
text:
<<the smugglers' scrawl>>

== readable fort_note
note: powder_room
intent: A note in the fort hinting at the money hidden behind the powder room.
text:
<<the fort's note>>

== readable harbourmasters_letter
note: way_up
intent: The harbourmaster's letter on his desk: why the seal matters (one of the keep's three), and what lies up the hill.
text:
<<the harbourmaster's letter>>

# The gate

== gate old_town
exits: to(old_town)
needs: seal
intent: The thief's thought when a way up turns them back without the seal.
text: <<turned back>>
